body:
Make a change to `eval_time` which increase to `3000000h`, the error is more deterministic. 

The cause is the change from `time.Duration` to `model.Duration`.  Related PR is https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/pull/6297.

The bug of this pr is that `time.ParseDuration` checks bigger integer overflow but `model.ParseDuration` not.

Another bug is that `time.Duration` is not equal to `model.Duration`,  the unit of `time.Duration`  is `ns`, the unit of `model.Duration` is `ms`.

```go
 Outer:                
     for _, testCase := range tg.PromqlExprTests {
         // mint type: time.Time
         // testCase.EvalTime: model.Duration
         got, err := query(suite.Context(), testCase.Expr, mint.Add(time.Duration(testCase.EvalTime)),  
```

@brian-brazil @codesome

@johncming

I agree with brian-brazil: The PR you mentioned (#6297) has been merged in June, but I was able to reproduce this as early as in 2.17.0 released in March.

Re: the error being "more deterministic" when you tweak the `eval_time` -- it's the `promtool` that has a bug and is not deterministic; there is no error in the test itself.
